01:21.206 --> 01:23.207
Damn it, what's wrong with the AC?

01:23.208 --> 01:25.293
<i>And don't forget, Quahog is expected</i>

01:25.294 --> 01:27.295
<i>to experience record-high
temperatures this week,</i>

01:27.296 --> 01:29.255
<i>according to our respected meteorologist</i>

01:29.256 --> 01:31.215
<i>Dr. Jessica Sturgess.</i>

01:31.216 --> 01:34.176
<i>Formerly known as Weather Girl
Aah-Ooh-Gah Knockerson.</i>

01:39.391 --> 01:41.309
Sir, could you please
roll down your window?

01:41.310 --> 01:43.894
I can't. I spilled honey on it
and it won't move.

01:43.895 --> 01:45.646
Please just step out of the vehicle.

01:48.317 --> 01:50.943
Sir, you were swerving back there.

01:50.944 --> 01:53.321
Plus, you're drowning in sweat.
Have you been drinking?

01:53.322 --> 01:55.990
No. I don't start drinking
till... until the drive home.

01:55.991 --> 01:57.658
Why are you slurring your words?

01:57.659 --> 01:59.744
Sorry, I had Cap'n Crunch for breakfast.

01:59.745 --> 02:02.204
The roof of my mouth is in shreds.

02:02.205 --> 02:04.499
I find that story relatable.

02:04.500 --> 02:06.042
You're free to go.

02:06.043 --> 02:08.502
Man, I can't believe
that cop thought I was lying.

02:08.503 --> 02:10.964
The only time I lie
is when I play poker.

02:10.965 --> 02:12.340
<i>It's make-or-break time.</i>

02:12.341 --> 02:14.550
<i>$75 million at stake.</i>

02:14.551 --> 02:16.052
<i>Betting starts with Peter Griffin.</i>

02:16.053 --> 02:18.179
<i>Ooh, he's not looking</i>

02:18.180 --> 02:20.723
<i>at much of anything right now.
And those mirrored sunglasses,</i>

02:20.724 --> 02:22.350
<i>not doing him any favors.</i>

02:22.351 --> 02:24.473
All in.

02:29.566 --> 02:31.138
Got to take this. It's my wife.

02:31.139 --> 02:32.778
Are you here?

02:37.070 --> 02:39.200
Okay, you two just hang out in the store

02:39.201 --> 02:40.618
while I return this keyboard.

02:40.619 --> 02:43.079
I'm going to watch
the older boys play<i> Fortnite,</i>

02:43.080 --> 02:46.207
because I'm not old enough
to play<i> Fortnite</i> myself.

02:46.208 --> 02:48.250
Hi. I'd like to return this keyboard.

02:48.251 --> 02:49.710
Was there something wrong with it?

02:49.711 --> 02:51.879
Well,
it said it was designed for writers,

02:51.880 --> 02:54.632
but when I sat down to work, it
just wasn't flowing through me.

02:54.633 --> 02:56.703
- Do you have a receipt?
- Uh, no.

02:56.704 --> 02:58.409
Can't you just look it up?

02:58.410 --> 03:00.554
Do you have the credit card
you used to pay for it?

03:00.555 --> 03:03.766
I actually paid using
store credit for another return.

03:03.767 --> 03:05.893
Do you have the original
packaging for the item?

03:05.894 --> 03:07.603
No. No, that's

03:07.604 --> 03:09.647
that's probably with the receipt.

03:11.400 --> 03:13.901
Manager who's
dishearteningly younger than me

03:13.902 --> 03:15.486
to the service counter, please.

03:15.487 --> 03:17.780
This better not be another overring.

03:17.781 --> 03:20.158
Corpowate's gonna have my ass.

03:25.414 --> 03:28.457
Well, we can probably throw out
this sunflower butter

03:28.458 --> 03:31.461
now that Stewie's classmate
with the peanut allergy died.

03:33.255 --> 03:35.923
Oh, there you are, Peter.
Listen, I need you to...

03:35.924 --> 03:37.425
Why are you so sweaty?

03:37.426 --> 03:39.093
The AC in my car broke.

03:39.094 --> 03:40.428
<i>Not</i> from the honey.

03:40.429 --> 03:42.471
And fat-guy sweat is like a battleship.

03:42.472 --> 03:44.974
Once it gets going,
you can't just turn it around.

03:44.975 --> 03:46.267
So until the weather cools off,

03:46.268 --> 03:48.436
you're gonna be dealing
with a slippery walrus.

03:48.437 --> 03:51.105
Now, if you'll excuse me,
I see a potential rival

03:51.106 --> 03:52.899
to my beach supremacy.

04:04.494 --> 04:05.870
Now?

04:05.871 --> 04:08.164
No, let them tire themselves out.

04:09.249 --> 04:10.958
Dad, what are we doing here?

04:10.959 --> 04:13.127
Now that I sweat all the time,

04:13.128 --> 04:16.339
it's just natural that I be
a very sweaty bomb defuser.

04:20.510 --> 04:22.470
Steady. You can do this.

04:22.471 --> 04:26.098
All you gotta do is remember the
song you learned in bomb school.

04:26.099 --> 04:27.850
♪ <i>Green is good and green is good</i> ♪

04:27.851 --> 04:30.269
♪ <i>And red is good and yellow is good</i> ♪

04:30.270 --> 04:31.855
♪ <i>And clip whatever you want.</i> ♪

04:33.732 --> 04:35.566
Now, who can tell me what he did wrong?

04:35.567 --> 04:37.318
He made up a song about cutting wires?

04:37.319 --> 04:39.143
He made up a song about cutting wires.

04:39.144 --> 04:40.947
Don't do that, guys.

04:45.035 --> 04:47.328
We now return to</i> Indiana Jones

04:47.329 --> 04:49.164
and the Temple Beth Shalom.

04:50.165 --> 04:51.874
You must be Mr. Jones.

04:51.875 --> 04:53.000
It's<i> Dr.</i> Jones.

04:53.001 --> 04:55.169
Oh, a doctor.

04:55.170 --> 04:57.631
You should meet my frumpy daughter.

04:58.757 --> 05:01.094
Wow. What are you all dressed up for?

05:01.095 --> 05:03.385
Well, thanks to my car's AC breaking,

05:03.386 --> 05:06.013
I've been asked to be
an overly sweaty Southern lawyer

05:06.014 --> 05:08.474
