with an injured back?

09:48.963 --> 09:50.672
Peter, I don't care.

09:50.673 --> 09:54.676
Well, time to live out my dream
of becoming a bodega cat.

09:54.677 --> 09:57.513
I'm between the breads.

10:01.518 --> 10:04.478
Again, I want to say I'm so glad
all of our schedules lined up

10:04.479 --> 10:06.522
so we can work together.
And, as a reminder,

10:06.523 --> 10:08.232
we've got New York on the line.

10:08.233 --> 10:10.567
New York, are you there?

10:10.568 --> 10:13.195
Stewie, is there anyone specific
on the line in New York?

10:13.196 --> 10:14.530
Brian,
you're just showing your ignorance.

10:14.531 --> 10:16.865
The phrase is, "New York on the line".

10:16.866 --> 10:18.050
<i>Hey, buddy,</i>

10:18.051 --> 10:19.391
<i>move that piece of junk!</i>

10:19.392 --> 10:20.494
<i>Go Mets!</i>

10:20.495 --> 10:22.704
And that's the best city we have.

10:22.705 --> 10:24.164
All right, so,
we've heard from New York.

10:24.165 --> 10:25.597
- What have you guys got?
- This,

10:25.598 --> 10:26.750
this can't be the meeting.

10:26.751 --> 10:29.002
New York, I'm gonna put you
on hold for a second.

10:29.003 --> 10:30.879
Brian, you're embarrassing us
in front of New York.

10:30.880 --> 10:32.506
Now get it together.

10:32.507 --> 10:35.175
All right, let's show them
the pitch video we put together.

10:37.011 --> 10:38.428
My name's Stewie,

10:38.429 --> 10:40.556
and this camera saved my life.

10:40.557 --> 10:43.016
I was born on the wrong side
of the tracks.

10:43.017 --> 10:45.060
My father made holes in belts,

10:45.061 --> 10:47.855
and my mother was
the Italian guy on a pizza box.

10:47.856 --> 10:50.524
The old man wanted me to go
into the family business.

10:50.525 --> 10:53.277
Hey! I don't hear any holes being holed!

10:53.278 --> 10:54.862
I want to make movies, Pa!

10:54.863 --> 10:56.446
Don't make me beat you

10:56.447 --> 10:59.449
with the instrument with which
I make holes in belts!

10:59.450 --> 11:01.285
It's called an awl, Pa!

11:01.286 --> 11:03.079
You son of a bitch!

11:04.414 --> 11:06.164
Ma! Do something!

11:06.165 --> 11:08.750
Frank, no!

11:08.751 --> 11:10.460
<i>Six months later,</i>

11:10.461 --> 11:13.380
<i>my old man died when they</i>
<i>canceled</i> The Tony Danza Show.

11:13.381 --> 11:15.382
<i>The one that was on during the day.</i>

11:15.383 --> 11:18.135
<i>Anyway, all that
is why I want to make a movie</i>

11:18.136 --> 11:20.930
<i>about a dog who joins a hockey team.</i>

11:24.392 --> 11:26.476
Morning, handsome.

11:26.477 --> 11:28.187
Mwah.

11:30.273 --> 11:33.817
Now, Lois, you have been accused
of an unwanted touching.

11:33.818 --> 11:35.351
- When?
- Just now.

11:35.352 --> 11:37.738
- Just before the flip.
- Uh, this is ridiculous.

11:37.739 --> 11:39.072
Lois, please.

11:39.073 --> 11:40.741
Now, the way this works is

11:40.742 --> 11:43.952
we simply gather information and
I make up my mind an hour ago.

11:43.953 --> 11:45.787
Peter, please tell us what happened.

11:45.788 --> 11:47.497
I'm sitting there at my desk,

11:47.498 --> 11:49.249
trying to watch porn on sites

11:49.250 --> 11:50.751
you guys haven't figured out yet,

11:50.752 --> 11:51.919
and

11:51.920 --> 11:53.670
she comes in and kisses me.

11:58.134 --> 12:01.678
Now, Barbara, the reason
you are here at Super HR

12:01.679 --> 12:04.765
is there's been an accusation
of unwanted touching

12:04.766 --> 12:08.101
and an overly sexualized
work environment.

12:08.102 --> 12:10.854
That's it. Peter,
no more working from home.

12:10.855 --> 12:12.856
I want you to go back to the office.

12:12.857 --> 12:16.026
Peter, how can the company
make this right?

12:16.027 --> 12:18.820
Bring back Lay's WOW chips with Olestra.

12:18.821 --> 12:22.282
Mr. Griffin, those chips
were recalled in the '90s

12:22.283 --> 12:24.785
for causing explosive diarrhea.

12:24.786 --> 12:26.203
You heard me.

12:26.204 --> 12:27.871
Mmm.

12:27.872 --> 12:29.419
So good.

12:30.458 --> 12:31.541
Uh-oh.

12:34.212 --> 12:36.714
All right, boys, get me up to speed.

12:43.136 --> 12:45.013
Brian! Chris!

12:45.014 --> 12:46.181
Stewie, what's the matter?

12:46.182 --> 12:47.557
Our Kickstarter...

12:47.558 --> 12:49.351
What? Did we not hit our goal?

12:49.352 --> 12:52.854
I also want to ask a question
without looking at the screen.

12:52.855 --> 12:55.775
Oh, oh, we hit it all right.

12:59.362 --> 13:00.487
Whoa.

13:00.488 --> 13:02.155
We actually have to make this thing.

13:02.156 --> 13:03.657
Gentlemen, it's time

13:03.658 --> 13:05.701
to start inappropriately
touching actresses

13:05.702 --> 13:07.202
on the casting couch.

13:07.203 --> 13:10.580
Okay, I have been made aware
of the allegations.

13:10.581 --> 13:13.876
Is there anything you can say
on your behalf?

13:14.919 --> 13:16.838
I'm trans?

13:16.839 --> 13:19.675
You just won HR.

13:26.347 --> 13:28.015
All right. Dishes washed,

13:28.016 --> 13:29.224
kids off to school,

13:29.225 --> 13:31.101
taking my boobs out of my bra.

13:32.645 --> 13:35.439
Alexa, play Mom Spa channel.

13:38.401 --> 13:39.693
All right, you're gonna have
to catch me up.

13:39.694 --> 13:41.361
I just stepped off a bird from Omaha,

13:41.362 --> 13:42.863
