13:42.864 --> 13:44.281
Whoa, whoa, whoa. Slow down.

13:44.282 --> 13:45.699
I don't have the bandwidth
for this right now.

13:45.700 --> 13:47.701
This is a lot for me to unpack,
honestly.

13:47.702 --> 13:49.369
Uh-huh, uh-huh.

13:49.370 --> 13:50.912
Well, I'm gonna have
to circle back with Ken

13:50.913 --> 13:52.289
to get it past the goal line.

13:52.290 --> 13:54.583
Unless, Wendy, do you want
to run it up the flagpole?

13:54.584 --> 13:56.376
Well, at the end of the day,
it is what it is.

13:56.377 --> 13:57.919
Look, look, look. Listen, listen.

13:57.920 --> 13:59.713
Look, listen, look,
look, listen, listen.

13:59.714 --> 14:01.465
Not to put too fine a point on it,

14:01.466 --> 14:03.550
but when push comes to shove,
look, listen, look.

14:03.551 --> 14:05.218
Okay, I'm gonna put a pin in this.

14:05.219 --> 14:07.763
I got to go crowd the gate so
people think I'm in first class,

14:07.764 --> 14:09.514
even though I'm in boarding group seven.

14:09.515 --> 14:11.475
Peter, for God's sake,

14:11.476 --> 14:13.602
can I not just have 15 minutes
of peace and quiet

14:13.603 --> 14:14.686
in my own kitchen?

14:14.687 --> 14:16.480
All right, I'll stay out of your way.

14:16.481 --> 14:19.942
I will simply do my work
and not say a word.

14:55.019 --> 14:57.604
Peter, we are gonna have to fi...

14:57.605 --> 14:59.189
<i>Attention, please,</i>

14:59.190 --> 15:02.150
<i>we are gonna begin pre-boarding
Flight 238 to Scottsdale,</i>

15:02.151 --> 15:04.611
<i>beginning with our first-class
and Prestige members.</i>

15:04.612 --> 15:06.572
Oh, that's me. I got to go.

15:09.367 --> 15:12.119
Scuse me, is there any way
I can get on the plane now,

15:12.120 --> 15:15.414
even though I'm in the seat
whose back touches the bathroom?

15:19.669 --> 15:21.962
Okay, welcome
to the first official table read

15:21.963 --> 15:24.422
for<i> The Untitled Kickstarter Project.</i>

15:24.423 --> 15:26.383
Chris will be on speakerphone
from down the hall,

15:26.384 --> 15:29.219
and, as a reminder, that may
result in a five-second delay.

15:29.220 --> 15:32.389
So, now to hand it over
to our writer extraordinaire,

15:32.390 --> 15:34.683
- Mr. Brian...
<i>- Hi, everyone!</i>

15:34.684 --> 15:36.059
There's the delay.

15:36.060 --> 15:38.478
- Brian Griffin, take it away.
- Thank you, Stewie.

15:38.479 --> 15:39.688
And before we get started,

15:39.689 --> 15:41.314
I would like to officially thank Stewie

15:41.315 --> 15:42.649
for spearheading this project,

15:42.650 --> 15:44.067
and I'd like to thank Chris

15:44.068 --> 15:46.236
for his help scouting all the locations.

15:46.237 --> 15:48.655
Now, scene one. We open on a suburban...

15:48.656 --> 15:49.906
<i>Aw, you're welcome, Brian!</i>

15:49.907 --> 15:51.408
<i>Happy to pitch in.</i>

15:51.409 --> 15:52.826
Yeah, speaking of scouting,

15:52.827 --> 15:54.411
you sure got good at scouting

15:54.412 --> 15:55.996
the location of the nearest Burger King.

15:55.997 --> 15:57.080
Okay, scene one.

15:57.081 --> 15:58.498
We open on a suburban home,

15:58.499 --> 16:00.667
where a party is in full swing.

16:00.668 --> 16:02.419
There is a knock at the...

16:02.420 --> 16:04.546
<i>I do like Burger King!</i>

16:04.547 --> 16:05.672
At the door.

16:05.673 --> 16:07.842
The teenage son answers it.

16:11.762 --> 16:15.182
<i>Well, if it isn't my favorite uncle.</i>

16:15.183 --> 16:17.058
Why-why did we give him the lead part?

16:17.059 --> 16:19.019
Chris, we're having
a little delay issue here,

16:19.020 --> 16:21.272
so try and come in a little sooner,
yeah?

16:25.026 --> 16:26.776
<i>Roger that.</i>

16:26.777 --> 16:29.613
Okay. The teenage son stares
at the man in the doorway,

16:29.614 --> 16:32.908
- and they exchange an intense...
<i>- Back so soon, Uncle Cornelius?</i>

16:32.909 --> 16:34.576
Okay, Chris, that was a little too soon.

16:34.577 --> 16:36.077
Bri... look,
what we're gonna do is, Brian...

16:36.078 --> 16:38.705
<i>Why didn't you come to my mom's funeral?</i>

16:38.706 --> 16:40.457
No, no, Chris,
we're pausing for a second.

16:40.458 --> 16:42.209
All right? Okay, okay, Brian,
here's what we're gonna do.

16:42.210 --> 16:45.045
You're going to slap the table
halfway through your line,

16:45.046 --> 16:47.297
and, Chris, when you hear
the slap on your end,

16:47.298 --> 16:48.465
that's when you talk.

16:48.466 --> 16:49.716
Everyone got that?

16:49.717 --> 16:50.843
Yes.

16:54.430 --> 16:55.889
<i>Yes.</i>

16:55.890 --> 16:58.308
Okay. Uncle Cornelius stands
in the doorway

16:58.309 --> 17:00.393
in stunned silence

17:00.394 --> 17:03.480
not knowing what to say but
knowing he should say something.

17:03.481 --> 17:06.274
<i>Well, do you have anything
to say for yourself?</i>

17:06.275 --> 17:08.401
- This is working.
- You're damn right I do!

17:08.402 --> 17:10.737
Uncle Cornelius slaps the table in anger

17:10.738 --> 17:12.906
as he walks across
to pour himself a gin and...

17:12.907 --> 17:16.576
<i>I'll return your pearl-handled
revolver one bullet at a time!</i>

17:16.577 --> 17:18.745
Okay, let's just shoot it. It all works.

17:18.746 --> 17:22.332
I just want to thank... everyone
for all their hard work today.

17:22.333 --> 17:24.210
<i>You're welcome!</i>

17:29.298 --> 17:30.715
What the hell?

17:33.135 --> 17:34.344
Oh, hi, Peter.

17:34.345 --> 17:35.929
Like what I've done with the place?

17:35.930 --> 17:37.847
I'm not sure what you<i> have</i> done.

17:37.848 --> 17:41.518
Well, since you decided to turn
our house into an office,

17:41.519 --> 17:43.812
I decided to make it
into a public work space

17:43.813 --> 17:45.819
for everyone to enjoy.

17:45.820 --> 17:47.148
Principal Shepherd?

17:47.149 --> 17:49.401
Oh, hey, Peter. John Shepherd
of Shepherd Marketing.

17:49.402 --> 17:51.278
Eye contact, firm handshake.

17:51.279 --> 17:52.612
We can put your logo on anything:

17:52.613 --> 17:54.656
a mug, a set of pens, a mug.

17:54.657 --> 17:56.199
I, uh... I don't have a logo.

17:56.200 --> 17:57.701
Funny you should say that,

17:57.702 --> 18:00.120
because our art department
could whip you something up.

18:00.121 --> 18:02.998
Hmm, let's see. Peter, Peter...

18:02.999 --> 18:04.124
Penis?

18:04.125 --> 18:06.167
Let's just fire up Windows 98.

18:06.168 --> 18:07.794
You like that, right on the mug?

18:07.795 --> 18:09.488
Uh, n-no. No, thank you.

18:09.489 --> 18:11.006
Lois, what do you think you're doing?

18:11.007 --> 18:12.966
Uh, I don't know what
you're talking about, Peter.

18:12.967 --> 18:16.177
Just creating
a nice work environment for you.

18:16.178 --> 18:19.306
For instance, I also piped in
easy listening music

18:19.307 --> 18:20.515
throughout the house.

18:20.516 --> 18:21.975
♪ <i>Doo doo doo...</i> ♪

18:21.976 --> 18:24.144
"Ode to My Family" by the Cranberries?

18:24.145 --> 18:26.980
Lois, you know once I hear that,
I can't get it out of my head.

18:26.981 --> 18:29.024
Don't worry. It's not the whole song.

18:29.025 --> 18:30.150
It's just the...

18:30.151 --> 18:32.152
♪ <i>Doo doo doo doo</i> ♪

18:32.153 --> 18:33.361
Part on repeat.

18:33.362 --> 18:34.863
That's the catchiest part!

18:34.864 --> 18:36.197
Well, you better get to work.

18:36.198 --> 18:38.033
It's already 9:15.

18:38.034 --> 18:40.493
Come on, Peter, focus. You can do this.

18:40.494 --> 18:42.537
♪ <i>Doo doo doo doo, doo...</i> ♪

18:42.538 --> 18:45.248
And... send.

18:45.249 --> 18:46.499
All right.

18:46.500 --> 18:49.545
Let's see what Griffin's been up to.

18:52.380 --> 18:56.134
Hmm. I've been saying that
to corporate for years.

18:56.135 --> 18:57.344
I got your mug, Peter.

18:57.345 --> 18:59.346
That'll be $59.99.

18:59.347 --> 19:00.680
I got a Square here,

19:00.681 --> 19:02.766
so we can take care
of the transaction in-house.

19:02.767 --> 19:04.434
Geez, seems kind of pricey.

19:04.435 --> 19:07.062
Well,
we could bring that down to $29.99,

19:07.063 --> 19:09.064
but you'd have to buy 4,000 of them.

19:09.065 --> 19:12.525
Fruit Baskets Covered in
Cellophane. How may I help you?

19:12.526 --> 19:16.446
Long, juicy bananas and melon balls.

19:16.447 --> 19:18.531
No,
I know you hadn't asked me a question.

19:18.532 --> 19:21.539
I was just thinking
about another part of my day.

19:21.540 --> 19:23.953
Okay! Fire drill!

19:23.954 --> 19:26.206
Everyone out in the hot sun for an hour,

19:26.207 --> 19:28.958
with no information
as to when we're coming back!

19:28.959 --> 19:30.794
Damn it, Lois. I can't take this!

19:30.795 --> 19:33.963
Huh. Maybe you'd be better off
working from your office.

19:33.964 --> 19:37.258
But I thought you'd like having
me around the house all day.

19:37.259 --> 19:38.551
I thought so, too, Peter.

19:38.552 --> 19:40.929
But maybe it was too
much of a good thing.

19:40.930 --> 19:44.057
You know I love you, but if
this marriage is gonna survive,

19:44.058 --> 19:46.601
I think you need to be gone
for most of it.

19:46.602 --> 19:49.062
I guess you're right.
When you look at it,

19:49.063 --> 19:51.398
most marriages are
just a couple hours a night.

19:51.399 --> 19:54.401
I'm sorry I was getting on
your nerves, being home so much.

19:54.402 --> 19:57.278
I'll call Bert and ask him if
I can come back to the office.

19:57.279 --> 19:58.405
Thank you, Peter.

19:58.406 --> 19:59.989
I love you so much.

19:59.990 --> 20:02.790
- I love you, too.
- Mmm.

20:02.791 --> 20:05.870
Hey, I went ahead and ordered
those 4,000 penis mugs for you.

20:05.871 --> 20:06.996
I don't want those.

20:06.997 --> 20:08.790
Well,
what am I supposed to do with them?

20:08.791 --> 20:11.252
May I propose a merger?

20:11.253 --> 20:16.380
♪ <i>The secret of my success</i>
<i>is I'm living.</i> ♪

20:23.597 --> 20:25.104
Wow, we did it.

20:25.105 --> 20:26.641
We actually made a movie.

20:26.642 --> 20:28.101
Yeah, I don't want to call this a movie.

20:28.102 --> 20:29.602
We made a film.

20:29.603 --> 20:31.312
We made a film, guys.

20:31.313 --> 20:36.151
And we even had $300,000
left over to buy snacks.

20:36.152 --> 20:40.447
"M-Movie snacks are very
expensive" is, is-is the joke.

20:40.448 --> 20:41.740
Here we go.

20:45.870 --> 20:47.829
This is garbage!

20:47.830 --> 20:50.210
I'm just happy for a night out.

20:52.376 --> 20:54.335
Now,
who can tell me what they did wrong?

20:54.336 --> 20:56.504
They were no-talent jerks
who made a Kickstarter movie?

20:56.505 --> 20:59.174
They were no-talent jerks who
made a Kickstarter movie.

20:59.175 --> 21:00.968
Don't do that, guys.